[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710979431","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103880#issuecomment-2710979431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103880","id":2710979431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hlkNn","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T15:26:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T15:26:37Z","body":"Please do not merge yet, I am writing many potential issues I'm seeing","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710979431/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711173142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103880#issuecomment-2711173142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103880","id":2711173142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hmTgW","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T16:31:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T16:31:58Z","body":"OK, I thought I had 2 seen two issues, but it's just 1. After a closer inspection there is nothing wrong with wait_for_pipeline (that I can see).\r\n\r\nAs for _wait_for_all_pipelines():\r\n\r\nIf `_wait_for_all_pipelines()` was deadlocking before this PR, then it was broken then and is still broken now.\r\n\r\n**Here's the issue afterwards:**\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid _wait_for_all_pipelines() {\r\n\tthread_local LocalVector<WorkerThreadPool::TaskID> tasks_to_wait;\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tMutexLock local_lock(local_mutex);\r\n\t\tfor (KeyValue<uint32_t, WorkerThreadPool::TaskID> key_value : compilation_tasks) {\r\n\t\t\ttasks_to_wait.push_back(key_value.value);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\t// <  !!! ERROR !!! more tasks may have been pushed to compilation_tasks here\r\n\r\n\tfor (WorkerThreadPool::TaskID task_id : tasks_to_wait) {\r\n\t\tWorkerThreadPool::get_singleton()->wait_for_task_completion(task_id);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\t// <  !!! ERROR AGAIN !!! more tasks may have been pushed to compilation_tasks here\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis code only works if there's a single writer, multiple readers. Or if it has been externally guaranteed that no other thread can possibly call `compile_pipeline` by the time we reach _wait_for_all_pipelines. However if it was deadlocking, that's a huge red flag.\r\n\r\nThe original version had the same problem, as new elements could be pushed after wait_for_task_completion(). Or could deadlock.\r\n\r\nAnother problem slightly unrelated with this PR I'm seeing is that `get_pipeline()` accesses `hash_map` for read without a mutex:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nRID get_pipeline(const Key &p_key, uint32_t p_key_hash, bool p_wait_for_compilation, RS::PipelineSource p_source) {\r\n\t\tRBMap<uint32_t, RID>::Element *e = hash_map.find(p_key_hash);\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever `hash_map` could be in the process of being written by another thread inside `_add_new_pipelines_to_map()`:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nbool _add_new_pipelines_to_map() {\r\n\tthread_local Vector<uint32_t> hashes_added;\r\n\thashes_added.clear();\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tMutexLock lock(compiled_queue_mutex);\r\n\t\tfor (const Pair<uint32_t, RID> &pair : compiled_queue) {\r\n\t\t\thash_map[pair.first] = pair.second; // <<---- Ooops\r\n\t\t\thashes_added.push_back(pair.first);\r\n\t\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**That is unless** get_pipeline() & clear_pipelines() are both guaranteed to be called from the main thread and the main thread only.\r\nAdditionally, the code must guarantee that it is impossible to call `compile_pipeline()` in another thread by the time we call `_wait_for_all_pipelines` (i.e. by the time we call clear_pipelines()).\r\n\r\nDocumentation says nothing about any of this and whether the class is single writer or multiple writers, etc. This is a nightmare to analyze.  It would also be clearer if the class [used guard macros](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ThreadSafetyAnalysis.html) to explain what variables are guarded, eg.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nRBSet<uint32_t> compilation_set GUARDED_BY(local_mutex);\r\nHashMap<uint32_t, WorkerThreadPool::TaskID> compilation_tasks GUARDED_BY(local_mutex); \r\n```\r\n\r\nPlus document which calls can be called by which threads, and what are the preconditions. However I suspect `_wait_for_all_pipelines` is just flawed and crosses fingers all threads that can issue `compile_pipeline()` are done by now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711173142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711530625","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103880#issuecomment-2711530625","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103880","id":2711530625,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hnqyB","user":{"login":"100gold","id":1216278,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTYyNzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1216278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold","html_url":"https://github.com/100gold","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/100gold/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T18:52:32Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T18:52:32Z","body":"Yes, there are issues about hash_map and _wait_for_all_pipelines external guarantees. But I made this PR to fix the deadlock between PilelineHashMapRD::local_mutex and GDScriptCache::mutex. I got callstack for the function wait_for_pipeline and I made changes in _wait_for_all_pipelines because it contains very similar code affected by the same problem, I think. Probably, it should be another ticket for those synchronization problems.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711530625/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711546668","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103880#issuecomment-2711546668","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103880","id":2711546668,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hnuss","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T18:58:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T18:58:09Z","body":"Ok t